WEBVTT

00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:02.480
To belong to no one.
To be no one else's power.

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:03.390
Letter of Marque
To belong to no one.
To be no one else's power.

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:04.350
To belong to no one.
To be no one else's power.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:07.770
To be your own person,
traveling space for your own benefit.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:11.240
That is what it means to be a
space pirate with a Letter of Marque.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.200
But now, a great danger has come upon them:

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.450
the pirate hunters.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.330
They possess a new kind of warship.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:23.870
It strikes down pirate ships, one after another,
with unmatched firepower and mobility.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.000
And now...

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.250
What is that?

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.010
The time has come!

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:37.010
What is it?

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:38.510
Hmm...

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:41.050
Transponder signal acquired.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:42.390
"Registered with the Galactic Empire.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:46.470
The great pirate ship that sails the
vastness of space: the Parabellum."

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:47.980
Huh? The what?

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.690
That's what's listed in their latest data.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:54.020
Basically, they're Galactic Empire pirates.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:58.110
I take that to mean they're a different kind of pirate altogether.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:01.570
A Galactic Empire pirate ship?

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:10.040
Hey, how is he standing outside without a spacesuit?

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.790
It's a hologram.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:15.460
The waving flag's a hologram too.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.380
They're also forcing sound effects
of flapping into the data stream.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:19.840
Pretty impressive trick.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:20.550
Why do all that?

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:22.010
To impress us.

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.430
Fire!

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:03.260
That's taking the sound effects too far!

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:05.260
You could really feel the bass!

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:07.390
Is he gonna save us?

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.890
Gravity waves rising in the enemy ship.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:11.640
Captain?

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.740
Enemy is withdrawing fast.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.870
Amazing acceleration.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:31.250
Incoming message.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.960
It's from the pirate ship Parabellum.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:34.830
Send it here.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.500
My name is Ironbeard!

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.260
Ironbeard?

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:45.260
Hey, have you ever heard of him, Schnitzer?

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:46.970
No, never.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.970
And this is my ship, the Parabellum.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:56.560
We hail from distant seas.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.610
Captain Ironbeard?

00:04:58.610 --> 00:04:59.900
Um...

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.860
Grave peril has come upon you.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:08.700
If nothing is done, all pirates in this region will soon be eliminated

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:12.950
at the hands of the pirate hunter vessel, the Grand Cross!

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:14.500
Grand Cross?

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:15.540
Was that the warship's name?

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:18.290
Searching

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:19.040
No Matches

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:22.420
No record of that ship anywhere.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:24.420
But there are records of the Parabellum.

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.380
"Registered with the Galactic Empire.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:29.430
The great pirate ship that sails the
vastness of space: the Parabellum."

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:30.510
We already heard that.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:44.070
Not that I care, but can't we do anything about that sound?

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.360
The Parabellum's forcing it into the data stream.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:49.530
It's funny, so I'm leaving it.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.490
Sound effects...

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:00.790
We need to hurry and rescue the Big Catch!

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:19.150
Ow...

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:20.560
Deal with it!

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:21.980
There are people here in worse shape.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:24.190
If you're a pirate, stop whining.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:31.910
Pretty pathetic.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.910
I'm sorry, Captain Stone.

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:37.660
We weren't able to protect your ship.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.750
We extinguished most of the fires,

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.540
but we couldn't keep them from
reaching the ammo stores.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:50.380
I guess my pirating days are over.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:52.470
What about my crew?

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:55.890
Everyone on the Big Catch is safe.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:58.390
A lot of people are hurt, though.

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:01.310
But our doctor says she'll save them all.

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:04.770
The bloodstained ship's doctor, Bloody Misa?

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:05.900
I'm glad to hear that.

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:07.570
You know Misa?

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:09.900
Not just Misa.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:13.120
I knew Blaster Ririka and Captain Kato too.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.530
They were good people.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:20.870
You're a good pirate, like your father.

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:23.920
Something in you shines.
Something an old man like me lacks.

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:27.420
You're a pirate for a new era.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:45.190
I'm Chiaki Kurihara.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.400
It's nice to meet you.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:16.680
Come on, Chiaki.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:19.060
You should just stay here.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:20.810
Let's graduate together.

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:23.140
I can't do that.

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:25.230
Could you try not to be so selfish?

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:27.400
So, what do you want?

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:35.870
I'm here as a representative of the captain.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:37.830
A representative?

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:45.420
I have a message from the captain of the
pirate ship Barbalusa, Kenjo Kurihara.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:49.880
Kenjo is worried about the damage
caused by the pirate hunters.

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:54.550
He's thinking of forming an alliance of
all pirates bearing Letters of Marque.

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:59.640
He requests help from the captain
of the Bentenmaru, Kato Marika.

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:06.400
I thought so.

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:11.610
We're compiling information from all
the pirates who have been attacked.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:17.910
The Bentenmaru has not only engaged them, you have battle data as well.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:19.830
First, we'd like to share that data.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:22.500
That isn't a problem.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:26.460
I'll give you everything we have on the
Grand Cross and the Parabellum.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.000
The Grand Cross?

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.040
What's that?

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:31.670
The seas of space...

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:32.840
Belong to everyone.

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:33.630
Come in!

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:38.300
This is the tea I was telling you about.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:41.100
Oh! It's the royal family's preferred tea!

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.060
Jeez...

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:47.690
You have a princess running errands and pouring tea?

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:49.440
This will be an international incident.

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:50.730
Don't worry about it.

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:55.950
Well, she's not a pirate, but I still think it might be good to ask her about it.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.490
Sure, I guess.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:04.080
So, I understand that the pirate hunters are
actually a warship called the Grand Cross.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.410
But what is the Parabellum?

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:07.790
An enemy? A friend?

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:09.960
Heck if I know.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.590
We encountered it, then it attacked.

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:15.630
Both ships showed up out of nowhere,
and then just disappeared.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:17.510
Well, that's true.

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:18.590
Perhaps...

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:23.760
The gravity-controlling ship that attacked the Bentenmaru

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:30.190
may have come from a higher-level area than any of the nearby governments, including Serenity.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.270
By higher level, you mean...

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:34.730
The Galactic Empire.

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:35.780
That's right.

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:39.240
An enormous Galactic Empire fleet appeared,

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:43.620
and absorbed both sides with its overwhelming power.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:49.920
Our nation has been unified as well.

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:53.790
But the Galactic Empire has always
pretended to ignore the pirates.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:11:00.050
The imperial fleets have never undertaken a large-scale offensive or any such pursuit against pirates.

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:02.430
And this is their offensive?

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:03.800
I don't know.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:08.930
We don't even know if the Grand Cross is an imperial ship.

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:13.190
Then you'll need my help.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.190
Please wait until after school.

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:20.990
I shall take appropriate measures to look into the Grand Cross and the Parabellum.

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:36.420
Welcome.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:37.210
What would you like?

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:38.800
A chocolate parfait.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:39.670
Same.

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:40.340
Me too.

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:43.340
Three chocolate parfaits!

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:49.770
I see.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.190
That does sound like a secret weapon.

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:58.360
The Galactic Empire is hurriedly constructing
large warships with gravity control.

00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:02.740
At least four companies are working on classified projects.

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:06.240
They're conducting trial runs on pirates in remote regions?

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:10.330
Well, it would provide more realistic data
than attacks on civilian or military ships.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:16.040
We can keep investigating its identity, but we should decide what to do about it first.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:17.630
So, Chiaki...

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:21.340
I agreed to share the data,
but what else do we have to do?

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:26.350
The legendary chef.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:28.060
Chef?

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:32.560
We need to find the legendary chef!

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:39.780
<i>Sing!</i>

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:40.570
<i>Drink!</i>

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:41.030
<i>Fight!</i>

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:12.680
Cheers!

00:13:15.340 --> 00:13:18.440
But why do we have to toast?

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:20.980
Because of what you said, Chiaki.

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:22.690
The legendary chef!

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:24.610
Come on, cheers!

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:25.900
Cheers!

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:35.250
This will be the first joint operation by pirates since the war of independence.

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:38.090
The key to achieving it will be the legendary chef—

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:39.540
Once more, cheers!
The key to achieving it will be the legendary chef—

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:43.050
Not that it matters,

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:45.420
but why are you wearing a maid outfit?!

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:47.010
Mami gave it to me.

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:48.910
Her again?

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:51.890
Yup!

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:59.920
It was the legendary chef who brought all the pirates to the table, whether they wanted to or not.

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:08.570
His many delicious dishes, and above all his sherbets,
melted the rough hearts of the pirates.

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:10.820
It's like a fairy tale.

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:12.330
So romantic.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:16.410
I'm sure his food was good.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:22.670
But the reason he could unite the pirates during the war of independence was because they trusted him.

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:27.340
Do you know why pirate ships still use old equipment?

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:29.390
Because we can't afford to upgrade?

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:31.180
That's part of it.

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:33.310
Indeed, the economy's been bad lately.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:42.310
But no matter how much money pirates make and what new parts they buy, they always leave the old comm systems.

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:43.650
The Bentenmaru's the same, right?

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:45.320
Look at these.

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:47.240
These gummy snacks are delicious.

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:50.160
They're nasty and squishy and so bad for you!

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:54.370
You're right, come to think of it.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:55.740
The same is true of the Odette II.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.630
The legendary chef.

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:07.920
He knows a song of summoning that causes all space pirates to tremble with anticipation.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:10.130
And that song is...

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:12.340
Hello?

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:15.260
The seas of space...

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:16.560
Belong to everyone.

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:20.230
What are those two doing here?

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:21.940
They came to celebrate your transfer.

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:27.070
I was planning on calling the whole yacht club, but that'll have to wait.

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:31.730
I'm here as the captain of the Barbalusa's
representative to see you, the Bentenmaru's—

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:32.620
Right, right.

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:33.660
I know. I know.

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:34.660
No, you don't!

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:39.410
Ever since you first mentioned it,
something has been bothering me.

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:42.420
And now that we've eaten the parfaits and made our toast, I'm sure of it.

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:48.210
Come with me tomorrow,
and I'll introduce you to the legendary chef.

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:54.930
Can we come in yet?

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:56.600
I said "Belong to everyone" already...

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:58.350
Oh, sorry!

00:15:58.350 --> 00:15:59.650
I'll open it right away.

00:15:59.650 --> 00:16:01.560
Oh, Marika.

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:21.370
Hello.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:24.580
You don't have a reservation today, I believe.

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.040
A Pirate's Council.

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:29.840
I want to hold a Pirate's Council.

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:33.010
H-He's the legendary chef?

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:35.340
What did you say?

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:37.640
I just remembered.

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:41.430
Ririka used to bring me here a lot.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:46.190
Like when I learned how to swim or ride a bike.

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:51.860
When I was little, any time I learned to do something,
she'd always let me have that one thing.

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:55.910
I don't need any more rewards.

00:16:57.490 --> 00:17:02.410
I want to eat dessert as an attendee of a Pirate's Council, not for a reward.

00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:08.130
I'm sure Ririka relied on you.

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:11.920
Ririka is an amazing person.

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:13.590
She's larger than life.

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:17.260
If she relies on you, you must be amazing too!

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:18.760
Don't try to flatter me.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:21.770
Your cooking is the best in space!

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:24.390
Even the pirates will listen to you.

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:26.350
How can you be sure?

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:27.690
Because I'm a pirate.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:32.230
In the name of the Bentenmaru.

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:57.840
You're a funny girl.

00:17:58.640 --> 00:17:59.260
Thanks.

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:01.260
Was it really that good?

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:02.220
Yup.

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:05.230
Your mother's that much larger than life?

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:06.440
Yes.

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:07.940
She's number one in space too!

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:15.070
Sorry, but you've got the wrong guy.

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:21.410
The legendary chef was my dad.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:33.710
It was an incredible sight.

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:37.250
All the famous pirates larger than life,

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:39.590
and all of them were shining.

00:19:00.920 --> 00:19:02.070
What is a pirate?

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:03.700
Power.

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:04.790
Power?

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:07.080
Force of arms? Violence?

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.830
The power to be in space.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:10.710
The power to be yourself.

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:16.960
I want to go into the wider universe.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:18.510
That's why I became a pirate.

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:35.730
Not what you expected?

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:36.570
Well...

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:37.730
No.

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:39.520
Good, you're honest.

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:47.200
<i>...the men and women.</i>

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:49.450
<i>Pirates are strong!</i>

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.620
<i>Drinking and fighting.</i>

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:53.460
<i>A pirate's soul!</i>

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:58.380
I thought I was hearing a weird
song from this comm unit,

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:00.510
and then it suddenly started up.

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:03.890
I was always told to never throw it out or mess with it.

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:05.890
So that's what it was for.

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:15.560
There it is.

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:23.240
Surrounded by asteroids, gas clouds, and stellar debris, it's the perfect hiding spot.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.490
Perfect for a pirate's nest.

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:29.830
Any pirates who hear this song might go to this place.

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:31.540
However, they also might not.

00:20:31.540 --> 00:20:32.580
But we're going, right?

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:36.000
If nothing else, the Barbalusa should be on its way.

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.340
No, it is.

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:40.340
Maybe not everyone will come.

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:46.340
But if they think of how things are now and what we have to do, they should understand when they hear this.

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:48.390
Let's go, mateys!

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:49.180
Roger!

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:54.810
Bentenmaru: our destination, the pirate's nest.

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:55.810
Full speed ahead!

00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:58.270
You look happy.

00:20:59.100 --> 00:20:59.780
Really?

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:13.040
Touchdown detected in front of us.

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:15.120
Hmm, this mass is...

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:16.750
It's them!

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:23.840
Displaying on main monitor.

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:26.930
That's it?

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:30.510
The Grand Cross.

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:04.970
